I go back to my table.
I look out of the window.
The people on the street are freezing.
I open my backpack.
I take my phone out.
I have three messages from my sister Sofia.
Sofia lives in Mexico.
There it is still early now.
I read the messages.
A few minutes later, the waiter comes.
He brings my order.
He puts the coffee on the table.
"Your coffee, here you go," the waiter says.
"And here is your chocolate cake," he then says.
The cake looks very good.
"Thank you very much," I say.
"You're welcome," the waiter answers.
